Aerie-Purpose: Put the "Archive Today tabs after" and "Keep archived tabs for" rows in the Sidebar section of Settings, let the settings page write the keep pref, and give the page its strings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private (prefs_util.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #183. The rows, settings-aerie-archive-after-row and settings-aerie-archive-keep-row, are Lit
elements in the overlay (chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/aerie_archive_*_row.*).
Each is a settings-dropdown-menu. The first writes aerie.tabs.archive_after (12h, 24h, 7d or never;
already in the settings_private allowlist since patches/sidebar/0010), the same pref the header
menu of the Archive panel writes. The second writes aerie.tabs.archive_keep (7d, 30d, 90d or
forever), added to the allowlist here as a string literal; a test compares it with
aerie_tab_model::kArchiveKeep. Both take effect without a restart. Their strings are in the
overlay's aerie_sidebar_strings.grdp, which patches/sidebar/0022 includes in generated_resources.grd;
this patch hands them to the page. The elements sit in the "Sidebar" section, under the
folder-rules row of patches/sidebar/0038.

